Diff rises from 1.50e-4 to 2.25e-4 over steps 1-13 (flagged by the policy), jumps to 4.18e-4 at step 15 (Ni-S n_d +1.6e-2, mspin -1.3e-2) and at step 20 (Ni-S-1 n_d +1.1e-2, mspin -8.1e-3); the other layers move by at most 2e-3 in those steps. No non-finite value. The Ni-S orbital moment rises from 0.117 to 0.173 with increments falling from 7.0e-3 to 1.0e-3 per step (not saturated at step 20); Ni-S-1 passes through 0.0523 at step 5-6 and falls to 0.0488; ES 5.7e-4 -> 7.4e-4. The cause of the excursions is not diagnosed (suspects: the unconverged host, Broyden history at beta 0.005, the slow orbital-moment mode); it was not investigated further.
